    "rationale": "Blocked on the compiler-resource fields required to justify a Tier-1 redesign. Reproducible public Metal pipeline queries and same-host end-to-end code-block-throughput workloads now populate every available field: static threadgroup bytes, SIMD width, maximum threads per group, and code-block throughput. Public Metal still does not expose registers per thread, private/local bytes, achieved occupancy, active SIMD groups, spill loads/stores, or cache counters. xctrace spill-event absence is not proof of no spilling, and the installed undocumented native translator was not accepted as reproducible evidence. CUDA compiler/runtime statistics also require the unavailable Linux/NVIDIA lane. No spill behavior is inferred from source scratch arrays and P7-P10 remain blocked."
